SUMMARY:Nest Box Building Workshop (Black Mountain)
DESCRIPTION:Lake Tomahawk in Black Mountain is a hotspot for wildlife particularly waterfowl with multiple species breeding and nesting along the edge of the lake. Join NCWF Swannanoa Valley Wild at Lake Tomahawk in Black Mountain for a nest box building workday. We’ll be primarily constructing and installing wood duck boxes. This is a fun family-friendly opportunity to support wildlife conservation on a grassroots level. We’ll meet under the shelter beside the tennis courts. See you there! \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/nest-box-building-workshop-black-mountain/
CATEGORIES:Featured
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncwf.org/wp-content/uploads/woodducks.jpg
END:VEVENT
