LAST-MODIFIED:20260903T190041Z
UID:10001776-1792602000-1792607400@ncwf.org
SUMMARY:Swannanoa Valley Wild Open Board Meeting (Black Mountain)
DESCRIPTION:Swannanoa Valley Wild is a local chapter of the North Carolina Wildlife Federation covering Black Mountain\, Swannanoa\, and Montreat. The chapter works to conserve wildlife and its habitat in the Swannanoa Valley area through community events like habitat restoration workdays\, educational programs\, and social gatherings. \nDo you have a passion for wildlife and habitat? Are you interested in volunteering and/or serving on the chapter’s leadership team? This is a great opportunity! Join us for an open board meeting at the Robertson Room at YMCA Blue Ridge Assembly in Black Mountain. We will be filling everyone in on the successes and challenges as we move forward as a chapter. The chapter has open leadership roles that we will discuss and open up for folks to apply. Protecting\, conserving\, and restoring wildlife and habitat is a big job and we need your help! \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/swannanoa-board-meeting/
CATEGORIES:Featured
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncwf.org/wp-content/uploads/boardmeeting.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Wildlife Federation
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261022T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261022T203000
DTSTAMP:20260827T150737Z
CREATED:20260827T150737Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260827T150737Z
UID:10001765-1792695600-1792701000@ncwf.org
SUMMARY:Beyond the Basics: Deer Hunting Start Smart: Gear\, Expectations & Tools That Work (Online)
DESCRIPTION:Join NCWF Fall Line Outdoors Chapter for a deer hunting webinar series! Build your core hunting skills and learn what it takes to start deer hunting. In this webinar we’ll cover licensure and NCWRC apprentice pathways\, hunting ethics\, every hunter’s conservation role\, time and cost commitments. We’ll also discuss choosing and fitting a weapon\, basic firearm care\, and a practical pack dump with essential gear. Then we’ll introduce advanced tools like rangefinders\, wind apps\, shooting sticks\, deer carts\, calls\, scents\, and decoys. You’ll leave with the skills and knowledge to begin your hunting journey with confidence. \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/deer-hunting-tools/
CATEGORIES:Featured
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncwf.org/wp-content/uploads/tools.jpg
END:VEVENT
